    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0194" n="88" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg88"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Señor
                            Guirola</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to apprise you, in
                    connection with the Department’s note of the 9th of February last, of the
                    receipt of a letter from the Secretary of the Treasury, of the 21st instant, in
                    relation to the threatened violation of the neutrality laws of the United
                    States. The statement is made by Mr. Foster, after due investigation by an
                    officer of his Department, that up to the present time no preparations have been
                    made at New York to disturb the peace in Central America, and there is no
                    likelihood of any such preparations.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
